course: dictionary
lesson: 14666
title: Too early
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Premature means happening or done too early, before the right time. Its first part, pre-, means before. «It's premature to celebrate before the match ends.» The game is not finished, so celebrating now is too early.
explain: Premature can also describe a baby who is born too early, before 37 weeks of pregnancy. «The premature baby stayed in a special hospital unit to grow stronger.» Babies born early often need extra care, such as an incubator, which keeps them warm and safe.
explain: A scientist who draws a premature conclusion jumps to an answer before there is enough evidence. Check the clues first, then decide. Waiting for the proof is not slow; it is careful.
fact: Premature means happening too early, before the right time.
fact: «Premature» can describe a baby born before 37 weeks of pregnancy.
fact: A premature baby is often cared for in an incubator in a special hospital unit.
fact: Pre- means before, so «premature» is about being too early.
fact: A premature conclusion is drawn before there is enough evidence.
exercise: «It's premature to celebrate before the match ends.» What does premature mean here? | Easy to understand | Very loud and happy | *Too early, before the right time | Late, after everyone has gone home
exercise: «The baby was born premature and stayed in an incubator to keep warm.» What kind of baby is this? | A baby who is older than her big brother | A baby born on a Sunday in the summer | A baby who cannot yet crawl | *A baby born too early, before 37 weeks
exercise: «The scientist made a premature conclusion before the tests were finished.» What does this suggest? | *She decided too early, before there was enough evidence | She asked her friends for help | She finished the tests very quickly and checked every result | She wrote a long report with lots of pictures
test: In «He made a premature guess», which word means most nearly the same as premature? | Slow | Certain | Careful | *Too soon
test: The first part of premature, pre-, means what? | *Before | Again | After | Not
exam: Leo says premature must mean late, the opposite of early. Is he right? | *No, premature means too early, before the right time | Yes, it means late, the opposite of early | Yes, it means happy and calm | No, premature means very old
